**/build
**/build-*
**/*~
**/.vscode

# Emacs autosaves (#file#) and lock files (.#file). An empty docs/#wi2.f#
# was tracked for a while: it slipped past docs/*.f below, because an
# autosave's name ends in # rather than in the extension it shadows.
**/#*#
**/.#*

# LaTeX build artefacts
docs/*.aux
docs/*.log
docs/*.out
docs/*.toc
docs/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/*.fls

# Local reference material: open-access papers kept in docs/ while the
# reference documentation is written. Not ours to redistribute, and not
# wanted in the history. canonical-components.pdf is ours and is tracked.
# Papers are ignored by default and our own documents are opted in, so a
# paper dropped into docs/ later is caught without anyone remembering to.
docs/*.pdf
!docs/canonical-components.pdf

# The same, for reference *source*: SLATEC's 3j routines were read while
# Schulten-Gordon was implemented (docs/3j-plan.md T6). SLATEC itself is
# public domain, but the F90 port that circulates is not necessarily, and
# either way it is not ours and the library derives nothing from it beyond
# the algorithm, which is the paper's. Keep it locally, out of the history.
docs/*.f
docs/*.f90
# wig2.f is Woodhouse's original and predates all of this; it stays.
!docs/wig2.f
!docs/gshtrans-reference.pdf
